IO-51: force the continuity tables on large negative errors too

DefaultReportPlugin writes the runoff, runoff quality, flow routing and
quality routing continuity tables when [REPORT] CONTINUITY is YES or when
the signed error exceeds 10 %, so a large negative error never forces them.
Compare the magnitude instead, and keep the runoff quality error of largest
magnitude rather than the largest positive one.

Requires: IO-50

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after IO-50_swmm600.patch:
    git apply IO-51_swmm600.patch

